// Sparkle.xcconfig
// Sparkle 2 auto-update configuration (TECH-SPEC §10, plan U11).
//
// SU_FEED_URL: the production Sparkle appcast feed, hosted by GitHub itself.
// release.yml publishes a complete signed `appcast.xml` as an asset on every
// release, and the `/releases/latest/download/` path is a permanent URL that
// always resolves to the newest release's copy — so publishing a release IS
// publishing the update, with nothing to edit by hand anywhere. GitHub 302s
// to objects.githubusercontent.com and serves it as application/octet-stream;
// Sparkle follows redirects and parses the bytes without checking the MIME
// type. If the feed ever moves, update the URL here, re-run
// `xcodegen generate`, AND ship a new build — existing installs keep checking
// whatever URL was compiled into them.
//
// SU_PUBLIC_ED_KEY: the PUBLIC half of a Sparkle EdDSA keypair generated
// locally via Sparkle's `generate_keys` tool (see SECRETS.md for exactly
// where the private half lives and how to export it for CI). Safe to
// commit — it's a public key used only to verify appcast signatures.

// NOTE: `//` begins a comment ANYWHERE in an xcconfig line, so a literal
// URL here would silently truncate to `https:`. The empty variable
// substitution `$()` below splits the two slashes without changing the
// resolved value — the standard xcconfig idiom for URLs.
SU_FEED_URL = https:/$()/github.com/nabeelhyatt/whistle/releases/latest/download/appcast.xml
SU_PUBLIC_ED_KEY = Y9Xz7q5K5r2Q3o4m/0UPgG9X+oU0zCujfMDbAdzabd4=
